   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5fca8c79aca10c0069e36e33",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/64bf6f26854d620d318d4082f2e6a6a7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FE-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/64bf6f26854d620d318d4082f2e6a6a7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FE-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/64bf6f26854d620d318d4082f2e6a6a7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FE-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/64bf6f26854d620d318d4082f2e6a6a7?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FE-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "eddie",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8c79aca10c0069e36e33",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "This is partly a bug in the installer, which creates the filter-mapping with a wildcard url-pattern regardless of install options. However, even if the installer is corrected to create individual filter-mappings for the various API-A/M servlets, there's still the problem of REST-API requests. That is, if API-A auth is false, then REST-API requests that map to API-A should not require authentication.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Notably, with the legacy authentication system, REST-API calls are differentiated via a special filter when API-A auth is false: fedora.server.security.servletfilters.FilterRestApiAuthn which explicitly checks for HTTP GETs and bypasses authN except for known API-M uri-patterns.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Seems like something similar would have to be done to AuthFilterJAAS. However, the workaround employed in FilterRestApiAuthn has the disadvantage that there's no way to further customize what requests should be allowed to pass without authentication. Moreover, there's the potential for authN settings for the SOAP API methods to get out of sync w/ the REST API methods.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
