      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Given the commits in r8467 to address this (the authnAPIA init-param for AuthFilterJAAS), should this be closed? Maybe the issue of the non-ideal nature of this solution should be logged as a separate issue.  Also closely related is FCREPO-521, which endeavors to get rid of the API-A/M distinction altogether in the Fedora APIs. That's likely a 4.0 thing, though.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
